From 01c96ecedc30fa0997fa6a6c53cc8a4e3e99183a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:22:36 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] recent_projects: a status bar button that opens a remote
 project
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.36 (ask 59), first half, from the operator's session
on Zeo 0.11.0 (2026-11-14). Zed reaches its remote projects modal through
the title bar's project menu or the command palette; the operator asked
for it beside the other status bar buttons.

RemoteProjectsButton (recent_projects/src/remote_projects_button.rs) is a
StatusItemView added to the left of the status bar, right after Project
Search: a Server icon whose tooltip names upstream's action, "Open Remote
Project", with its binding, and whose click dispatches upstream's own
`projects::OpenRemote` -- from_existing_connection false, create_new_window
None, so the chosen project opens where the user's default open behaviour
says, exactly as the menu entries do. The button adds no behaviour of its
own.

A new setting, `status_bar.remote_projects_button` (default true), hides
it; it is in default.json, StatusBarSettings, the settings window's Status
Bar section ("Remote Projects Button"), and the status bar's own
right-click "Hide" writes it through hide_setting. The VS Code import,
which builds StatusBarSettingsContent field by field, leaves it None (VS
Code has no equivalent).

The second half of §6.36 -- the order of the status bar's panel buttons,
set in the settings window -- is a separate patch.

Tests: remote_projects_button::tests (hiding writes the setting false; the
button opens the modal in this window; it shows by default). Seen failing
with the hide writer set to true. The settings, settings_content and
settings_ui packages pass with the new field. Xvfb proof:
docs/assets/zeo-6.36-remote-button-2026-11-15/ in the hub.
---

